  "notes": [
   "LOD0 only: LOD1 / LOD2 keep the merged Body.",
   "kind: door | hood | trunk | bumper | mirror | glass | lens | lamp. A node with a parent moves with it (and falls off with it).",
   "hinge_axis + open_sign: rotating by open_sign * angle (radians, right-handed about the axis) opens the panel; limits_deg = [0, max opening].",
   "lens / lamp: lamps lists the Headlight_* / Taillight_* empties the unit lights; a broken lens darkens its lamp node (emission off) and those lights."
  ]
 },
 "traffic": {
  "class": "sports",
  "spawn_weight": 0.7,
  "player": true
 },
 "notes": [
  "Calipers are separate nodes (Caliper_XX, same origin as Wheel_XX): steer them with the wheel but don't spin them. LOD2 has no calipers.",
  "Collider is a convex hull (extras: collider=convex, hidden=true): use it as a ConvexPolygonShape3D and hide the mesh.",
  "Headlight_* / Taillight_* empties: put a SpotLight3D / OmniLight3D there; their local -Z is the beam direction.",
  "Variants: glTF KHR_materials_variants on Body (all LODs). Godot does not apply the extension by itself: tools/vehicles/godot/vehicle_variants.gd reads it at import and offers set_variant(root, name).",
